# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""analysis.py -- Conformational Free-Energy Surface of the ACE-CYS-NME
capped dipeptide in vacuum at T = 300 K via Well-Tempered Metadynamics
(AMBER ff14SB, OpenMM Reference platform).

This file ships as a design-only deliverable because OpenMM cannot be
installed in the sandbox that produced it (verified offline, no wheels,
no apt/conda/mamba, source build blocked by missing
gfortran / fftw / boost / swig).

Organisation:

  (1) Pure-NumPy library -- Hill, gaussian_2d_periodic, reconstruct_bias,
      wt_correct, smooth_periodic, find_minima.  These run wherever any
      recent numpy is available.

  (2) OpenMM-backed driver main_simulate_and_analyse.  Raises
      RuntimeError(...) if openmm is not importable; otherwise is the
      real workflow that produces non-placeholder artefacts.

  (3) Placeholder-mode writers used when run as the top-level script
      in a sandbox without OpenMM: fes_2d.npy is zeros (72,72) float64;
      minima.csv is header-only; fes_plot.png is a blank-axes PNG with
      the title banner; cv_definition.txt is the (3) phrasing prepended
      with the STATUS banner; README_INCOMPLETE.txt is the (4) banner.

  (4) self_test_reconstruction() -- a synthetic-hill self-test that
      exercises reconstruct_bias + wt_correct + find_minima.  Runs
      unconditionally and prints PASS / FAIL.

  (5) main() -- runs the self-test always; if openmm is importable it
      delegates to main_simulate_and_analyse; otherwise it falls through
      to placeholder writers.
"""
from __future__ import annotations
import csv
import math
import os
import sys
from dataclasses import dataclass
